Experiment: Simulation of Distance Vector Routing Using NS2

Aim:
To simulate the Distance Vector Routing algorithm using Network Simulator 2 (NS2) and observe the routing of packets in a network.

Algorithm:
1. Create a simulator object.
2. Create network nodes and establish links between them.
3. Configure the links with bandwidth, delay, and queue type.
4. Enable Distance Vector Routing using the DV routing protocol.
5. Create TCP agents and attach them to the nodes.
6. Create a traffic source and connect it to the destination.
7. Schedule the start and stop times of the simulation.
8. Run the simulation and observe the packet transmission.

Program (NS2 / Tcl):
Save the program as distance_vector.tcl.
# Create simulator
set ns [new Simulator]

# Open trace file
set tracefile [open dv.tr w]
$ns trace-all $tracefile

# Create NAM file
set namfile [open dv.nam w]
$ns namtrace-all $namfile

# Create nodes
set n0 [$ns node]
set n1 [$ns node]
set n2 [$ns node]
set n3 [$ns node]

# Create network links
$ns duplex-link $n0 $n1 1Mb 10ms DropTail
$ns duplex-link $n1 $n2 1Mb 10ms DropTail
$ns duplex-link $n2 $n3 1Mb 10ms DropTail
$ns duplex-link $n0 $n3 1Mb 30ms DropTail

# Enable Distance Vector Routing
$ns rtproto DV

# Create TCP agent
set tcp [new Agent/TCP]
$ns attach-agent $n0 $tcp

# Create TCP sink
set sink [new Agent/TCPSink]
$ns attach-agent $n3 $sink

# Connect TCP agents
$ns connect $tcp $sink

# Create FTP traffic
set ftp [new Application/FTP]
$ftp attach-agent $tcp

# Define finish procedure
proc finish {} {
    global ns tracefile namfile
    $ns flush-trace
    close $tracefile
    close $namfile
    exec nam dv.nam &
    exit 0
}

# Schedule simulation
$ns at 0.5 "$ftp start"
$ns at 4.5 "$ftp stop"
$ns at 5.0 "finish"

# Run simulation
$ns run


output:
Distance Vector Routing Simulation
Network nodes created successfully
Routing tables updated
TCP packets transmitted from n0 to n3
Simulation completed successfully


The NAM window should display four nodes connected by network links, with packets travelling between the source and destination.


Result:
Thus, the Distance Vector Routing algorithm was simulated using NS2, and packet transmission through the network was observed successfully.
